Testing Swift sources on Ubuntu failed deeply within clang::RawComment segmentation faults on all provided swift-6.0.1 and swift-5.10.1 distributions via swift.org, blocking swift test. The requirement evaluation has been analyzed statically through the codebase sources instead since runtime evaluation could not be safely executed. Mac framework reliance (Darwin, SystemConfiguration, BPF, XCTest, etc) also precludes Linux-based testing.
